\paragraph{Iteration and cognitive models of writing.}
Iterative generation methods improve text through repeated feedback and revision~\citep{madaan2023self,du2022iterative}, while cognitive writing research offers a process-level account of how planning, drafting, and reviewing interact~\citep{flower1981cognitive,hayes1996new,hayes2012modeling}.
\citet{gero2022design} use those processes to organize writing-support systems, and CogWriter~\citep{wan2025cognitive} likewise draws on cognitive writing theory to structure planning, generation, and revision.

replacements.after:
\paragraph{Iteration and cognitive models of writing.}
Iterative generation methods improve text through repeated feedback and revision~\citep{madaan2023self,du2022iterative}, and PEER~\citep{schick2023peer} trains a model to imitate the writing process by proposing and explaining edits, while cognitive writing research offers a process-level account of how planning, drafting, and reviewing interact~\citep{flower1981cognitive,hayes1996new,hayes2012modeling}.
\citet{gero2022design} use those processes to organize writing-support systems, and CogWriter~\citep{wan2025cognitive} likewise draws on cognitive writing theory to structure planning, generation, and revision.

\paragraph{Evaluator dependence.}
Section~\ref{sec:results-effectiveness} complements the order-consistent win rates with unconditional and worst-case missing-output views.
The primary evaluator belongs to the same model family as the generator, and related generator--judge models can exhibit preference leakage or self-preference~\citep{li2026preference,panickssery2024selfpreference}.

\paragraph{Component attribution.}
The ablations constrain explicit goals and adaptive ordering to modest contributions without establishing equivalence.
Neither ablation differs from the full system in any benchmark--run test after Holm correction, each such test reaches 80\% power at a true preference of about \PowerCellDetectablePreference, and the exploratory prompt-level summary does not rank the two components.\footnote{See Appendix~\ref{app:prompts} for the power calculation.}
\condFixedOrder\ enforces its cycle through the \texttt{Monitor}'s instructions so that it shares our system's agent runtime and differs only in the selection rule, and \AsixCycleCompliantRate\ of its paths are cycle-compliant.\footnote{See Appendix~\ref{app:process-behavior} for the trace classification.}
Next steps are a runner-enforced cycle and a combined ablation that removes goals and fixes the order together, which would test whether the two mechanisms substitute for each other.

\paragraph{Execution variants.}
\condSingleWriter\ changes delegation, role context, decision granularity, and output length together; \condSingleContext\ is narrower but was added post-hoc, uses one exploratory generation run, and differs in execution interface and transport.

